   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the building inspector in the town of Pendleton, county of\nNiagara, to reside outside such town",
    "basePrintNo": "S3620",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3620-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3620\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nauthorizing the building inspector in the town of Pendleton, county of\nNiagara, to reside outside such town\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow the building inspector for the town of Pendleton to reside\noutside the Town.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 Adds a new subdivision 35 to section 23 of the town law to\nallow the building inspector for the town of Pendleton to reside outside\nthe Town.\n\nSection 2 adds a new subdivision 71 to section 3 of the public officers\nto allow the building inspector for the town of Pendleton to reside\noutside the Town.\n\nSection 3 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation, which is at the request of the town, would allow them\nthe opportunity to hire a building inspector who is not a resident. The\ntown is in desperate need of hiring a qualified building inspector, and\nthe town reports an extreme shortage of viable candidates who reside\ninside the town. This legislation will ensure public safety by allowing\na qualified building inspector to be hired, regardless of location.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.872 of 2023-2024; Referred to Local Government\n\nS. 3630A of 2021-2022; Referred to Local Government\n\nS.126 of 2019-2020: Referred to Local Government.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
